--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -4,6 +4,41 @@ A sign-in sheet for Lansing tech events.
 
 https://lansingcodes.github.io/sign-in-sheet/
 
+## Digital sign-in prototype
+
+`digital/` is a separate Netlify Forms prototype for issue #14. The existing
+printable sheet remains at the site root. The optional `event` query parameter
+pre-fills the event field, for example
+`/digital/?event=Lansing%20Codes%20Meetup`; use that URL to make a QR code for
+the welcome slide. Attendees can edit the event name, so organizers should
+review it before using submissions as an attendance record.
+
+### Move it to a Lansing Codes account
+
+1. Merge CI PR #18, then this prototype PR. Create a Netlify site owned by
+   Lansing Codes, connect this repository, set the publish directory to the
+   repository root (`.`), and leave the build command empty. A manual deploy
+   of the same static files also works.
+2. In the new site's **Forms** page, enable form detection and deploy again.
+   Check that Netlify lists the `meetup-sign-in` form.
+3. Open `/digital/` on the new site. Submit one fictional record, check the
+   custom success page, and confirm the record appears in the private Forms
+   dashboard. Keep the newsletter box unchecked for that test.
+4. Set the approved attendee notice, form access and retention policy. Check
+   the site's free-plan limits. Only then make a QR code for the new site's
+   event-specific `/digital/?event=...` URL and use it at a meetup.
+
+GitHub Pages can serve the HTML but cannot process the Netlify form. If the
+site stays on GitHub Pages, a separate managed form or backend is required.
+
+The form collects a name, optional email, and an unchecked newsletter-interest
+flag. It does **not** subscribe anyone automatically. A checked interest flag
+requires an email in the browser. Netlify stores submissions in the site's
+private Forms dashboard, accessible to its team members. The honeypot reduces
+basic automated submissions. This is a demonstration: use fictional data on a
+personal test site. Before using it with attendees, settle consent wording,
+access, retention, deletion, spam controls, and the newsletter handoff.
+
 ## Code of Conduct
 
 All participants are expected to treat others with respect and follow our [Code of Conduct](https://www.lansing.codes/code-of-conduct/).
diff --git a/digital/index.html b/digital/index.html
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0ceb22b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/digital/index.html
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+  <head>
+    <meta charset="utf-8">
+    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
+    <title>Meetup sign-in prototype · Lansing Codes</title>
+    <link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css">
+    <script defer src="script.js"></script>
+  </head>
+  <body>
+    <main>
+      <div class="brand">Lansing <strong>Codes</strong></div>
+      <p class="eyebrow">Digital sign-in prototype</p>
+      <h1>Welcome to the meetup.</h1>
+      <p class="intro">Sign in for today’s event. This prototype uses a private Netlify Forms inbox; organizers would need to deploy it under a Lansing Codes account before accepting real attendee details.</p>
+      <p class="demo">For testing, enter fictional details only.</p>
+      <form name="meetup-sign-in" method="POST" action="/digital/thanks.html" data-netlify="true" netlify-honeypot="bot-field">
+        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="meetup-sign-in">
+        <p class="honeypot"><label>Leave this field empty <input type="text" name="bot-field" autocomplete="off"></label></p>
+        <label for="event">Event</label>
+        <input id="event" name="event" type="text" maxlength="100" required value="Lansing Codes meetup">
+        <label for="attendee-name">Your name</label>
+        <input id="attendee-name" name="attendee-name" type="text" autocomplete="name" maxlength="100" required>
+        <label for="email">Email <span>(optional)</span></label>
+        <input id="email" name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" maxlength="254">
+        <label class="choice"><input id="newsletter" name="newsletter" type="checkbox" value="yes"> I’d like to receive the Lansing Codes monthly newsletter.</label>
+        <p class="privacy">Your name and any email you provide are used to record attendance for this event. Newsletter interest is separate and unchecked by default. A real deployment needs an organizer-approved privacy and retention policy.</p>
+        <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
+      </form>
+      <p class="paper">Prefer paper? Ask an organizer for the printed sign-in sheet.</p>
+    </main>
+  </body>
+</html>
diff --git a/digital/script.js b/digital/script.js
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a4bb581
--- /dev/null
+++ b/digital/script.js
@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+const eventName = new URLSearchParams(window.location.search).get('event');
+if (eventName && eventName.trim().length <= 100) {
+  document.querySelector('#event').value = eventName.trim();
+}
+
+document.querySelector('#newsletter').addEventListener('change', (event) => {
+  const email = document.querySelector('#email');
+  email.required = event.target.checked;
+});
